== B. finite differences
PASS dEx/dz = -mu dHy/dt (lossless, forward)
PASS -dHy/dz = eps dEx/dt (lossless, forward)
PASS lossy: dEx/dz = -mu dHy/dt
PASS lossy: -dHy/dz = sigma Ex + eps dEx/dt
PASS lossy telegrapher 1: -dV/dz = L dI/dt
PASS lossy telegrapher 2: -dI/dz = C dV/dt + G V
PASS G/C = sigma/eps and LC = mu eps
PASS forward V = f(t - z/v), I = +f/Z0 satisfies telegrapher
PASS backward V = g(t + z/v), I = -g/Z0 satisfies telegrapher
PASS control: backward with I = +g/Z0 violates telegrapher
PASS V = f + g, I = (f - g)/Z0 satisfies telegrapher
PASS d2V/dz2 = LC d2V/dt2
PASS quadrature antiderivative gives I = +C v f = f/Z0 (forward)
PASS quadrature antiderivative gives I = -f/Z0 (backward)
PASS C v = 1/Z0 and L/Z0 = sqrt(LC)
PASS Z0 = Ex d/(Hy W) = eta d/W
== C. directions (np.cross)
PASS plate 2 (x=0): rho_s = n.D = +1 eps Ex
PASS plate 2 (x=0): J_s = n x H = +z Hy
PASS plate 1 (x=d): rho_s = n.D = -1 eps Ex
PASS plate 1 (x=d): J_s = n x H = -z Hy
PASS forward: E x H along +z
PASS backward (V>0, I<0): E x (-y) along -z
PASS loop up at z, back down at z+dz has right-hand normal -y
PASS emf V(z)-V(z+dz) = -dPsi/dt (Psi along -y) = +mu d dz dHy/dt  | emf=-9.4503e-07, -dPsi/dt=-9.4503e-07
PASS plate-2 charge per metre rho_s W = eps Ex W = C V
== D. geometrical factors
PASS coax C = eps GF, GF = 2pi/ln(b/a)
PASS coax L = mu/GF
PASS coax LC = mu eps
PASS twin-lead: wire surfaces are equipotentials (images at +-s)
PASS twin-lead C = pi eps / acosh(D/2a)  | C/eps=2.00510, GF=2.00510
PASS twin-lead L = (mu/pi) acosh(D/2a)
PASS twin-lead LC = mu eps
PASS twin-lead thin-wire limit ln(D/a) vs acosh(D/2a) differ at D/2a = 2.5  | ln(D/a)=1.6094, acosh=1.5668
PASS Rao Table 6.1 (wire spacing 2d): pi eps/acosh(d/a) == page form
PASS Z0 = eta/GF = sqrt(L/C) for coax
PASS Z0 = eta/GF = sqrt(L/C) for twin-lead
